Title: THE CLOCKWORK DRYAD
Genre: Animation / Fantasy
Recommended Style: Anime Cinematic (Studio Ghibli) & Pixar Pre-vis

EXT. ANCIENT MOSS-COVERED FOREST - SUNSET
[STYLE: Anime Cinematic | PALETTE: Lush Verdant Emeralds, Golden Sunbeams, Luminous Spores]

Sunlight filters through ten-thousand-year-old cedar boughs in radiant golden god-rays. Floating bioluminescent moss spirits drift like glowing green fireflies.

LUMI (10, oversized mechanic's goggles, denim overalls, leather satchel) kneels beside the roots of the Great Elder Tree.

Embedded in the tree trunk is a moss-covered brass clockwork heart with spinning cogwheels and crystal gears.

LUMI
(whispering)
Hold still, little dryad. Just one more winding turn.

Lumi inserts a silver winding key into the brass gear.

CLICK. WHIRRRRR.

The ancient tree trunk SHIVERS. Glowing amber sap flows through the bark like electrical circuitry. A pair of luminous emerald eyes open within the wooden bark!

DRYAD (O.S.)
(musical chime voice)
Thank you, daughter of the clockmaker. The forest has been asleep for three hundred winters.
